## Context

rtk on **padme** went 0.42.1 -> 0.49.0 on 2026-09-16, and gained an
`exclude_commands` block in `~/.config/rtk/config.toml`. That file is **not
version-controlled and not shared between machines**, so neither half of the fix
has reached doudou. Until it does, a session there measures through a filter
whose defects were established on padme the same day:

- Below 0.45.0 a redirection to a file does **not** dodge the rewrite — the hook
  is PreToolUse and rewrites the command string before any shell sees the `>`.
  `git log -5 > f` came back 1447 bytes against 5946, with every `Merge:` line
  gone.
- At 0.42.1 the pytest filter announced **"Pytest: No tests collected"** for a
  run that collected four and passed three. Not a truncation, a false statement.
  0.49.0 fixes it and reports "3 passed, 1 failed".
- At 0.49.0, still: `rtk git log` drops every `Merge:` line (1596 bytes against
  4924), and `rtk make` truncates head-first past ~2 kB, so a test runner's
  verdict — which pytest prints in the tail — disappears. A 120-test green run
  showed no count at all; a red one hid two of its three failures.

The version on doudou has **not been measured**. Step 1 measures it; do not
assume it matches padme's former state.

## Relevant files

- `~/.config/rtk/config.toml` — per-machine, not in git. The artifact this
  ticket installs. On padme it now reads
  `exclude_commands = ["git log", "git status", "^make\\b.*\\bcheck\\b"]`.
- `rules/workflow.md` § Diagnosis discipline — the resident rule this implements
  ("Which shapes the proxy rewrites is a version fact, not a rule").
- `rules/git.md` § Reading state you will act on — the two rtk bullets.

## Actions

1. Record the installed version: `rtk --version`, and the binary's mtime.
2. Upgrade:
   `curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rtk-ai/rtk/refs/heads/master/install.sh | sh`
   Take the stable release, never a `dev-*-rc.*` pre-release.
3. `rtk config --create` if `~/.config/rtk/config.toml` is absent, then set
   `exclude_commands` in the `[hooks]` section to padme's list above.
4. Re-run the verification below **on doudou** — padme's results do not transfer.

## Test

Red first, and the red step is the point: **before** writing the config, run
`rtk hook check "git log -5"`. It must report a rewrite (`rtk git log -5`). If it
already reports "No rewrite", the config is present or the command is spared for
some other reason, and the rest of this ticket needs re-reading before it is
applied. A verification whose pass is indistinguishable from "I could not look"
is not a verification.

## Verification

- [x] `rtk --version` reports 0.49.0 or later. Observed: `rtk 0.49.0`, at
      `~/.local/bin/rtk` (install.sh, checksum verified); the cargo-installed
      0.45.0 that shadowed it in PATH was removed with `cargo uninstall rtk`.
- [x] `rtk hook check` discriminates (doudou, 2026-09-16): `No rewrite for:` on all
      four spared shapes; `rtk grep -n N f`, `rtk git diff HEAD`, `rtk make build`,
      `rtk make lint` on the four control shapes. Original criterion: **no rewrite** for `git log -5`,
      `git status`, `make check`, `make check-fast`; **still rewritten** for
      `grep -n N f`, `git diff HEAD`, `make build`, `make lint`. Both arms
      matter — an exclusion list that spares everything is not a test.
- [x] A bare `git log -5` contains `Merge:` lines and is ~4x the byte count of
      the pre-config output. Observed on doudou: bare 2110 bytes with 2 `Merge:`
      lines; `rtk git log -5` 936 bytes with 0. A 2.3x ratio on this repo's
      top-5, the `Merge:` loss is the same defect as on padme.
- [x] A deliberately failing `make check` names every failing test and prints the
      `N failed, M passed` summary. Observed on a scratch Makefile (4 green, 2 red):
      `FAILED test_a.py::test_red`, `FAILED test_b.py::test_red2`,
      `2 failed, 4 passed in 0.19s`; `rtk hook check` reported `No rewrite` for it.
- [x] `rtk pytest <a file with 3 green and 1 red>` reports "3 passed, 1 failed",
      not "No tests collected". Observed: `Pytest: 3 passed, 1 failed` followed by
      `1. [FAIL] test_red`.

## Invariants

- **Do not exclude `grep`.** It is 123 M tokens, 24.6 % of total savings on
  padme's census, and its `N matches in M files` header is accurate. Its cost is
  a truncated listing and paths rewritten to `/.../`, which fail loudly when
  used.
- **Do not exclude `pytest`** on 0.49.0 or later. The filter is honest there and
  excluding it taxes every test run. It was excluded on padme only while 0.42.1
  was lying, and removed once measured.
- Exclude only the `check*` make targets, not `make` wholesale.
- The config is machine-local by design. Do not try to commit it into the harness
  repo; record in this ticket what each machine ended up with.

## Exit criteria

- [x] doudou runs rtk 0.49.0 or later.
- [x] `~/.config/rtk/config.toml` on doudou carries the `[hooks]`
      `exclude_commands` list, with a comment naming the measurement behind each
      entry. Same three entries as padme.
- [x] Every box under Verification is ticked with the observed output pasted or
      quoted, not asserted.
- [x] A log entry here records doudou's before/after version and the date.
